    {
      "index": 5,
      "id": "method",
      "heading": "Method",
      "chunks": [
        {
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "chunk_id": "s05_c01",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s05_c1_how_test_works_candidate_change",
          "text": "Here is how the test works. At each candidate change point, it compares the pooled transition dynamics before and after that time using a CUSUM-style statistic.",
          "expected_role": "content",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "how",
            "test",
            "works",
            "candidate",
            "change",
            "point",
            "compares",
            "pooled",
            "transition",
            "dynamics"
          ],
          "required": true
        },
        {
          "chunk_index": 2,
          "chunk_id": "s05_c02",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s05_c2_naively_plugging_modern_machine_lear",
          "text": "Naively plugging modern machine-learning estimators into this comparison introduces heavy bias, so the authors add a mean-zero augmentation term, producing a doubly robust estimating function.",
          "expected_role": "content",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "naively",
            "plugging",
            "modern",
            "machine-learning",
            "estimators",
            "comparison",
            "introduces",
            "heavy",
            "bias",
            "authors"
          ],
          "required": true
        },
        {
          "chunk_index": 3,
          "chunk_id": "s05_c03",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s05_c3_lets_flexible_models_like_neural",
          "text": "That lets flexible models like neural networks and random forests estimate the transition and state-action distributions without spoiling the inference.",
          "expected_role": "method",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "lets",
            "flexible",
            "models",
            "like",
            "neural",
            "networks",
            "random",
            "forests",
            "estimate",
            "transition"
          ],
          "required": true
        },
        {
          "chunk_index": 4,
          "chunk_id": "s05_c04",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s05_c4_sample_splitting_cross_fitting_norma",
          "text": "Sample splitting and cross-fitting normalize the statistic across candidate points and test functions, and a Gaussian multiplier bootstrap approximates its null distribution to yield the final p-value. The maximum over time and test functions of the normalized, CUSUM-weighted statistic gives the test statistic gamma-hat.",
          "expected_role": "method",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "sample",
            "splitting",
            "cross-fitting",
            "normalize",
            "statistic",
            "across",
